---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PluginTabs from '../../components/PluginTabs.astro';
import { disciplines } from '../../lib/plugins.js';
import data from '../../data/cloudtak.json';

const plugins = data.plugins;
const developers = new Set(plugins.map((p) => p.owner)).size;
const used = Object.keys(disciplines).filter((k) => k !== 'all' && plugins.some((p) => p.tags.includes(k)));
const count = (k) => plugins.filter((p) => p.tags.includes(k) || (k !== 'tools' && p.tags.includes('all'))).length;
// Two-letter mark for the icon tile, e.g. "Quick Point Dropper" -> "QP".
const initials = (n) => n.split(/[\s/-]+/).filter((w) => /^[A-Za-z0-9]/.test(w)).slice(0, 2).map((w) => w[0].toUpperCase()).join('');
const month = (iso) => iso && new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---
<Base title="CloudTAK Plugins" description="Community plugins for CloudTAK, the browser TAK client: weather, search and rescue planning, printing, drones, cameras and more. Free, with the source on GitHub.">
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="page-head">
        <PluginTabs active="cloudtak" />
        <h1>CloudTAK Plugins</h1>
        <p>Plugins for <a href="https://github.com/dfpc-coe/CloudTAK">CloudTAK</a>, the TAK client that runs in a browser, built by responders and developers across the community. Free, with the source on GitHub. {plugins.length} plugins from {developers} developers.</p>
      </div>

      <section class="market">
        <div class="market-body">
          <span class="repo-tag">Easiest way in</span>
          <h2>Install them from TAK Portal’s Marketplace</h2>
          <p>Plugins marked <strong>Marketplace</strong> install, update and uninstall from the CloudTAK Marketplace in <a href="https://github.com/ValleyTacticalSolutions/TAK-Portal">TAK Portal</a>, on the server that runs CloudTAK. It pulls each plugin from its author’s repository and rebuilds CloudTAK for you. <a href="/infra-tak/">infra-TAK</a> sets up TAK Portal and CloudTAK together.</p>
          <div class="dl-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/ValleyTacticalSolutions/TAK-Portal">TAK Portal on GitHub</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/infra-tak/">infra-TAK install guide</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by discipline">
        <button type="button" class="chip" aria-pressed="true" data-f="*">All <span>{plugins.length}</span></button>
        {used.map((k) => (
          <button type="button" class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-f={k} style={`--c: ${disciplines[k].c}`}><i></i>{disciplines[k].label} <span>{count(k)}</span></button>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="plug-grid">
        {plugins.map((p) => (
          <a class="plug-card ct-card" href={`https://github.com/${p.repo}`} data-tags={p.tags.join(' ')}>
            <span class="plug-icon mono" style={`--c: ${disciplines[p.tags[0]]?.c ?? 'var(--accent)'}`} aria-hidden="true">{initials(p.name)}</span>
            <span class="plug-top">
              <h3>{p.name}</h3>
              <span class="plug-by">by {p.ownerName}{p.release && <span class="ver"> · {p.release}</span>}</span>
            </span>
            <p>{p.description}</p>
            <span class="plug-tags">
              {p.tags.map((t) => disciplines[t] && <span style={`--c: ${disciplines[t].c}`}><i></i>{disciplines[t].label}</span>)}
            </span>
            <span class="plug-meta">
              {p.marketplace && <span class="mk">Marketplace</span>}
              {p.server && <span>Has a server part</span>}
              {p.region && <span>{p.region}</span>}
              {p.license && <span>{p.license}</span>}
              {p.updated && <span>Updated {month(p.updated)}</span>}
            </span>
            <span class="ct-cta"><span class="ct-repo">github.com/{p.repo}</span>Learn more on GitHub →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="empty-note" hidden>No plugins tagged for that discipline yet.</p>

      <h2 class="section-title"><b>?</b> Installing without the Marketplace</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>CloudTAK builds its plugins into the web app, so a plugin is not a file you upload. Copy or link the plugin’s folder into your CloudTAK source (<code>app/plugins/&lt;name&gt;</code>, or <code>api/web/plugins/&lt;name&gt;</code> on older versions), then rebuild CloudTAK. A plugin with a <strong>server part</strong> also adds API routes or its own service, so the API needs a rebuild too.</p>
        <p><strong>Each plugin’s README has the exact steps and the CloudTAK versions it supports.</strong> Read it first: the plugin API is still young and changes between CloudTAK releases.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section-title"><b>+</b> Built one?</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Send it to the Marketplace with <strong>Submit a plugin</strong> in TAK Portal’s CloudTAK Marketplace, or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/ValleyTacticalSolutions/TAK-Portal/issues">TAK Portal</a>. Once it is in the Marketplace catalog, it shows up on this page by itself.</p>
        <p>Starting from scratch? <a href="https://github.com/dfpc-coe/CloudTAK-Plugin-Sample">CloudTAK-Plugin-Sample</a> is the official template, and <a href="https://github.com/jpat-12/CloudTAK-Plugin_Development">CloudTAK Plugin Development</a> is a community guide to how plugins work.</p>
        <p class="section-note">TAKwerx’s own CloudTAK plugins are on the <a href="/takwerx/#cloudtak">TAKwerx page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var chips = document.querySelectorAll('.filters .chip');
      var cards = document.querySelectorAll('.plug-card');
      var empty = document.querySelector('.empty-note');
      function apply(f) {
        var shown = 0;
        cards.forEach(function (c) {
          var t = c.dataset.tags.split(' ');
          var on = f === '*' || t.indexOf(f) >= 0 || (f !== 'tools' && t.indexOf('all') >= 0);
          c.hidden = !on; if (on) shown++;
        });
        chips.forEach(function (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(c.dataset.f === f)); });
        empty.hidden = shown > 0;
      }
      chips.forEach(function (c) {
        c.addEventListener('click', function () {
          apply(c.dataset.f);
          history.replaceState(null, '', c.dataset.f === '*' ? location.pathname : '#' + c.dataset.f);
        });
      });
      var h = location.hash.slice(1);
      if (h && document.querySelector('.chip[data-f="' + h + '"]')) apply(h);
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
